<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Eureka yr profit shrinks, declares div.</title>
<headline>Eureka yr profit shrinks, declares div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Feb 28</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre non-operating items  125.6  vs  125.5</p>
<p>    - after non-operating	125.6  vs  184.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			25.0   vs  nil</p>
<p>    Retained income		2.41   vs  4.43</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			  2.83   vs  3.39</p>
<p>    Tax				0.19   vs  0.38</p>
<p>    Funding costs		  1.55   vs  1.03</p>
<p>    Non-operating items	  nil    vs  1,42</p>
<p>    Turnover			 28.08  vs  32.55</p>
<p>Div payable</p>
<p>on register Dec 13</p>
<p>Full name: Eureka Industrial Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it was seeking alternative areas of investment where its expertise and resources can best be utilised. But it said that until such opportunities materialise no substantial change in the group's performance can be expected.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
